 "caveat": "Ocean and weather layers describe the sea, not what any vessel does. Expected activity says where lit boats or radar candidates usually are, given the sea and the weather; a cell above or below it is a lead for review, not evidence. Dark = no AIS match. Not evidence of illegal activity.",
 "limits": [
  "MUR is a merged multi-sensor analysis (ERDDAP comment: 'Multi-Resolution Variational Analysis (MRVA) method for interpolation'); where cloud hides the sea its 1 km detail is interpolated, so fronts on such days are likely smoother than reality (not quantified)",
  "front thresholds are relative (window quantiles of this sea's gradient), not an absolute front strength",
  "DINEOF chlorophyll is gap-filled; chl_valid_share says how often a direct retrieval anchored it",
  "RTOFS currents are depth-averaged (barotropic) model output, not surface currents; the SSH gradient is used as a proxy for eddy edges, not as a detection",
  "waves and wind are model fields at 0.25 degree, bilinear at cell centres",
  "no political boundaries in any layer; region names are reporting boxes"
 ],
 "not_used": [
